  "notes": "{分岐|ぶんき} describes the point where something splits into two or more paths. Used both literally (roads, railways, rivers) and figuratively (decisions, turning points in life).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {分岐|ぶんき}{点|てん}: branching point, turning point\n- {分岐|ぶんき}する: to branch, to fork, to diverge\n- {分岐|ぶんき}{路|ろ}: forked road\n- {分岐|ぶんき}{器|き}: splitter (technical device)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe figurative meaning of \"critical juncture\" or \"turning point\" is very common: {人生|じんせい}の{分岐|ぶんき}{点|てん} (turning point in life), {運命|うんめい}の{分岐|ぶんき}{点|てん} (turning point of fate).\n\nFORMS:\n{分|ぶん} (divide) + {岐|き} (fork, branch). The kanji {岐|き} specifically means \"branching path\" and also appears in {岐路|きろ} (crossroads).",
